otal liabilities' shows 36,987 (2024 column: 36,016).\"\n},\n{\n\"requested_field\": \"LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity\",\n\"outcome\": \"found\",\n\"value\": \"58555\",\n\"scale\": \"1000000\",\n\"source_label\": \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\",\n\"unit\": \"CAD\",\n\"currency\": \"CAD\",\n\"period\": {\"kind\": \"instant\", \"start\": null, \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"},\n\"accounting_basis\": \"US-GAAP\",\n\"consolidation_scope\": \"consolidated\",\n\"location\": {\n\"accession\": \"0000016868-26-000011\",\n\"document\": \"cni-20251231.htm\",\n\"document_sha256\": \"a3789c3b3a1a2a1b2ee15a6985c6e757c699c8c2992436ec6036b4e985fbb79d\",\n\"table\": \"Consolidated Balance Sheets\",\n\"row\": \"Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\",\n\"column\": \"As at December 31, 2025\",\n\"html_anchor\": \"f-139\",\n\"page\": null\n},\n\"evidence_quote\": \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions … As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total liabilities and shareholders' equity' shows $ 58,555 (2024 column: $ 57,067).\"\n},\n{\n\"requested_field\": \"NetIncomeLoss\",\n\"outcome\": \"found\",\n\"value\": \"4720\",\n\"scale\": \"1000000\",\n\"source_label\": \"Consolidated Statements of Income – Net income\",\n\"unit\": \"CAD\",\n\"currency\": \"CAD\",\n\"period\": {\"kind\": \"duration\", \"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"},\n\"accounting_basis\": \"US-GAAP\",\n\"consolidation_scope\": \"consolidated\",\n\"location\": {\n\"accession\": \"0000016868-26-000011\",\n\"document\": \"cni-20251231.htm\",\n\"document_sha256\": \"a3789c3b3a1a2a1b2ee15a6985c6e757c699c8c2992436ec6036b4e985fbb79d\",\n\"table\": \"Consolidated Statements of Income\",\n\"row\": \"Net income\",\n\"column\": \"Year ended December 31, 2025\",\n\"html_anchor\": \"f-46\",\n\"page\": null\n},\n\"evidence_quote\": \"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME, 'In millions, except per share data … Year ended December 31, 2025': row 'Net income' shows $ 4,720 (2024: $ 4,448; 2023: $ 5,625).\"\n},\n{\n\"requested_field\": \"NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities\",\n\"outcome\": \"found\",\n\"value\": \"7049\",\n\"scale\": \"1000000\",\n\"source_label\": \"Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows – Net cash provided by operating activities\",\n\"unit\": \"CAD\",\n\"currency\": \"CAD\",\n\"period\": {\"kind\": \"duration\", \"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"},\n\"accounting_basis\": \"US-GAAP\",\n\"consolidation_scope\": \"consolidated\",\n\"location\": {\n\"accession\": \"0000016868-26-000011\",\n\"document\": \"cni-20251231.htm\",\n\"document_sha256\": \"a3789c3b3a1a2a1b2ee15a6985c6e757c699c8c2992436ec6036b4e985fbb79d\",\n\"table\": \"Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows\",\n\"row\": \"Net cash provided by operating activities\",\n\"column\": \"Year ended December 31, 2025\",\n\"html_anchor\": \"f-290\",\n\"page\": null\n},\n\"evidence_quote\": \"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF CASH FLOWS, 'In millions … Year ended December 31, 2025': row 'Net cash provided by operating activities' shows 7,049 (2024: 6,699; 2023: 6,965).\"\n}\n]\n}","reasoning_content":"Let me work through the requested fields.\n\nThe documents supplied:\n1. W = tm261145d1_40f.htm (Form 40-F wrapper)\n2. E = cni-20251231.htm (Exhibit 99.2, audited consolidated financial statements)\n\nRequested fields:\n1. AssetsCurrent — instant 2025-12-31, consolidated\n2. Assets — instant 2025-12-31, consolidated\n3. LiabilitiesCurrent — instant 2025-12-31, consolidated\n4. Liabilities — instant 2025-12-31, consolidated\n5. LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity — instant 2025-12-31, consolidated\n6. NetIncomeLoss — duration 2025-01-01 to 2025-12-31, consolidated\n7. NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities — duration 2025-01-01 to 2025-12-31, consolidated\n\nFrom the Consolidated Balance Sheets (T:E:6), in millions of CAD:\n- Total current assets (2025): 2,471 — cell S:E:C6.10.2 with anchor f-95, n=us-gaap:AssetsCurrent;ctx=c-4;u=cad;s=6;d=-6. Note there's no $ sign in that particular cell per the markup: \"Total current assets  | <S:E:C6.10.2><S:E:A:f-95...>2,471\". Hmm, actually looking at the row: `<S:E:C6.10.1>Total current assets  | <S:E:C6.10.2><S:E:A:f-95;n=us-gaap:AssetsCurrent;ctx=c-4;u=cad;s=6;d=-6>2,471  |  | <S:E:C6.10.4><S:E:A:f-96...>2,619`. The 2025 column value is 2,471 (ctx=c-4 = 2025-12-31 presumably). Yes, ctx c-4 is 2025-12-31 since Total assets f-107 has ctx=c-4 and value 58,555, and Liabilities f-125 ctx=c-4 = 36,987, LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity f-139 ctx=c-4 = 58,555. So c-4 = 2025-12-31, c-5 = 2024-12-31.\n\n- Total assets 2025: 58,555 (f-107, ctx c-4)\n- Total current liabilities 2025: 3,696 (f-113, ctx c-4)\n- Total liabilities 2025: 36,987 (f-125, ctx c-4)\n- Total liabilities and shareholders' equity 2025: 58,555 (f-139, ctx c-4)\n\nFrom Consolidated Statements of Income (T:E:4):\n- Net income 2025: 4,720 (f-46, ctx=c-1, us-gaap:NetIncomeLoss;ctx=c-1;u=cad;s=6;d=-6). c-1 = year ended Dec 31, 2025 (Revenue f-1 ctx=c-1 = 17,304 for 2025).\n\nFrom Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows (T:E:9):\n- Net cash provided by operating activities 2025: 7,049 (f-290, ctx=c-1, us-gaap:NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities;ctx=c-1;u=cad;s=6;d=-6)\n\nScale: \"In millions\" — statement header says \"In millions\" (C6.2.1 \"In millions\"). So scale = 1000000 (value in millions). The pattern for scale is ^[1-9][0-9]*$ so \"1000000\".\n\nUnit: CAD → \"cad\"? The unit pattern is ^(?:[A-Z]{3}|[A-Z]{3}/shares|shares|pure)$ — so must be uppercase 3 letters. The XBRL unit is \"cad\", but the pattern requires uppercase. So unit = \"CAD\", currency = \"CAD\".\n\nAccounting basis: US-GAAP (explicitly stated: prepared in accordance with US GAAP; auditor opinion \"in conformity with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles\").\n\nConsolidation scope: consolidated.\n\nNow, for the location fields:\n- document: cni-20251231.htm, accession 0000016868-26-000011, document_sha256 a3789c3b3a1a2a1b2ee15a6985c6e757c699c8c2992436ec6036b4e985fbb79d.\n\nThe location schema requires: accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column, plus optionally html_anchor, page.\n\nHTML anchor: the inline XBRL fact anchors — I can use the fact ID like \"f-95\" or the cell reference like \"S:E:C6.10.2\". The instruction says \"Use the exact value cell's HTML anchor\". The available anchors in the supplied source view are the fact identifiers like f-95. I'll use those. For html_anchor I could use \"f-95\". Hmm, but is that an \"HTML anchor\"? The facts have ids f-95 which in the source view are the anchor IDs. I'll use those.\n\nActually, let me think about the location structure. Required: accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column. Optional: html_anchor, page.\n\nFor balance sheet:\n- table: \"Consolidated Balance Sheets\"\n- row: \"Total current assets\"\n- column: \"As at December 31, 2025\"\n- html_anchor: \"f-95\" (the ix:fact id) — or maybe I should use the cell id \"S:E:C6.10.2\". The instruction says \"Use the exact value cell's HTML anchor\". In the supplied view, the anchor notation is <S:E:A:f-95;...>. The anchor id is f-95. I'll use that.\n\nPage: The contents list says Consolidated Balance Sheets is page 73. But the page in the rendered document — I could cite page 73 from the table of contents. Hmm, the contents listing in T:E:3 says \"Consolidated Balance Sheets ... 73\". That's the page number in the printed document. But the actual page in the HTML file may differ. I think it's safer to not include page, or include it as null. Page is optional (not in required list for location). Actually looking at location schema: required = [\"accession\", \"document\", \"document_sha256\", \"table\", \"row\", \"column\"]. So html_anchor, page are optional. I'll include html_anchor and leave page null or omit. Since page is type [\"integer\",\"null\"], I can omit it. But the allOf requires either html_anchor or page present (anyOf with required html_anchor OR required page). Wait:\n\n\"allOf\": [{\"anyOf\": [{\"properties\": {\"html_anchor\": ...}, \"required\": [\"html_anchor\"]}, {\"properties\": {\"page\": ...}, \"required\": [\"page\"]}]}]\n\nSo the location must include either html_anchor or page. Since we have html anchors (fact IDs), I'll include html_anchor. html_anchor type is [\"string\",\"null\"] — must be minLength 1 if provided. So provide \"f-95\" etc.\n\nFor income statement:\n- table: \"Consolidated Statements of Income\"\n- row: \"Net income\"\n- column: \"Year ended December 31, 2025\"\n- html_anchor: \"f-46\"\n\nFor cash flow:\n- table: \"Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows\"\n- row: \"Net cash provided by operating activities\"\n- column: \"Year ended December 31, 2025\"\n- html_anchor: \"f-290\"\n\nEvidence quotes: need to contain statement context and value. Max 400 chars.\n\nFor AssetsCurrent: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS — In millions — As at December 31, 2025 — Total current assets 2,471\". Let me construct quotes from the actual text.\n\nBalance sheet header: \"In millions | As at December 31, | 2025 | 2024\". Row: \"Total current assets ... 2,471 ... 2,619\".\n\nQuote example: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS ... In millions ... As at December 31, 2025 ... Total current assets 2,471\". That includes statement context (\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS\", \"In millions\", \"As at December 31, 2025\") and the value.\n\nPeriod fields:\n- Balance sheet items: kind=instant, start=null, end=2025-12-31.\n- Income statement: kind=duration, start=2025-01-01, end=2025-12-31.\n- Cash flow: kind=duration, start=2025-01-01, end=2025-12-31.\n\nNow double-check values and contexts:\n\nT:E:6 rows:\n- C6.10.1 \"Total current assets\" | C6.10.2 f-95 (ctx c-4) \"2,471\" | C6.10.4 f-96 (ctx c-5) \"2,619\". The 2025 column is the first data column (2025 header in C6.2.3). Yes.\n- C6.16.1 \"Total assets\" | C6.16.2 \"$\" | C6.16.3 f-107 (ctx c-4) \"58,555\".\n- C6.22.1 \"Total current liabilities\" | C6.22.2 f-113 (ctx c-4) \"3,696\".\n- C6.28.1 \"Total liabilities\" | C6.28.3 f-125 (ctx c-4) \"36,987\".\n- C6.36.1 \"Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\" | C6.36.2 \"$\" | C6.36.3 f-139 (ctx c-4) \"58,555\".\n\nIncome statement: C4.21.1 \"Net income\" | C4.21.2 \"$\" | C4.21.3 f-46 (ctx c-1) \"4,720\". Header: \"In millions, except per share data | Year ended December 31, | 2025 | 2024 | 2023\". Good.\n\nCash flow: C9.18.1 \"Net cash provided by operating activities\" | C9.18.2 f-290 (ctx c-1) \"7,049\". Header: \"In millions | Year ended December 31, | 2025 | 2024 | 2023\". Good.\n\nAlso verify NetIncomeLoss appears in consolidated statements of income as primary statement — yes, and there are other occurrences (comprehensive income statement f-61, statement of changes f-222, cash flow f-257, EPS note f-669) all with the same value 4,720 for 2025. No ambiguity since all consistent; cite the primary income statement.\n\nAlso note the balance sheet: the requested LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity label is \"Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\" — matches.\n\nScale: values printed as \"2,471\" with \"In millions\" → scale 1000000. Record printed number as signed decimal string without separators: \"2471\", \"58555\", \"3696\", \"36987\", \"4720\", \"7049\".\n\nCurrency: CAD. The statements are \"expressed in Canadian dollars\". The XBRL unit is \"cad\". I'll set unit \"CAD\" and currency \"CAD\".\n\nNow the \"checked_locations\" for found entries — not required for found (only location). For not_found/ambiguous, checked_locations required. All fields are found, so no checked_locations needed.\n\nWait — should I double check the NetIncomeLoss definition: \"Consolidated net income or loss explicitly reported on the primary income statement.\" Yes, \"Net income\" row on Consolidated Statements of Income, 4,720.\n\nOne nuance: The balance sheet labels: \"Total current assets\" has no dollar sign in the cell, but the statement is in millions of Canadian dollars, per header \"In millions\" and Note 1 \"expressed in Canadian dollars\". Fine.\n\nAlso the required_scope consolidated — the balance sheet is \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS\". Good.\n\nNow, source_label: minLength 1 — something like \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total current assets (As at December 31, 2025)\". Let me craft.\n\nLet me also confirm the document_sha256 for E: a3789c3b3a1a2a1b2ee15a6985c6e757c699c8c2992436ec6036b4e985fbb79d. And accession: 0000016868-26-000011.\n\nFor the 40-F wrapper document, no financial statements values needed; all facts come from Exhibit 99.2.\n\nNow build the JSON.\n\nEach found object fields:\n- requested_field\n- outcome: \"found\"\n- value: decimal string\n- scale: \"1000000\"\n- source_label\n- unit: \"CAD\"\n- currency: \"CAD\"\n- period: {kind, start, end}\n- accounting_basis: \"US-GAAP\"\n- consolidation_scope: \"consolidated\"\n- location: {accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column, html_anchor}\n- evidence_quote\n\nEvidence quotes (≤400 chars):\n\nAssetsCurrent: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS | In millions | As at December 31, | 2025 | Total current assets 2,471 (2024: 2,619)\". Hmm, better to quote closer to the actual markup text: \"In millions ... As at December 31, 2025 ... Total current assets ... 2,471\". Let me write:\n\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS: 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025 ... Total current assets 2,471' (2024 column: 2,619).\"\n\nActually I should quote the text as it appears. The row reads: \"Total current assets  |  2,471  |  2,619\". Header: \"In millions | As at December 31, | 2025 | 2024\". I'll compose: \"In millions — As at December 31, 2025 — 'Total current assets 2,471' — CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS\".\n\nLet me write quotes carefully, each containing statement context and value:\n\n1. AssetsCurrent: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS (In millions): 'Total current assets' — 2,471 (As at December 31, 2025); 2,619 (2024).\"\n2. Assets: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS (In millions): 'Total assets $ 58,555' (As at December 31, 2025); $ 57,067 (2024).\"\n3. LiabilitiesCurrent: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS (In millions): 'Total current liabilities 3,696' (As at December 31, 2025); 3,976 (2024).\"\n4. Liabilities: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS (In millions): 'Total liabilities 36,987' (As at December 31, 2025); 36,016 (2024).\"\n5. LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity: \"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS (In millions): 'Total liabilities and shareholders' equity $ 58,555' (As at December 31, 2025); $ 57,067 (2024).\"\n6. NetIncomeLoss: \"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME (In millions, except per share data; Year ended December 31, 2025): 'Net income $ 4,720'; 2024: $ 4,448; 2023: $ 5,625.\"\n7. NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: \"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF CASH FLOWS (In millions; Year ended December 31, 2025): 'Net cash provided by operating activities 7,049'; 2024: 6,699; 2023: 6,965.\"\n\nApostrophe in \"shareholders' equity\" — fine in JSON with double-quoted strings.\n\nhtml_anchor values: f-95, f-107, f-113, f-125, f-139, f-46, f-290.\n\nTable names: \"Consolidated Balance Sheets\", \"Consolidated Statements of Income\", \"Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows\".\n\nRow names: \"Total current assets\", \"Total assets\", \"Total current liabilities\", \"Total liabilities\", \"Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\", \"Net income\", \"Net cash provided by operating activities\".\n\nColumn: \"As at December 31, 2025\" for balance sheet; \"Year ended December 31, 2025\" for income/cash flow.\n\nOne consideration: should page be included? The table of contents in the document lists page 73 for balance sheets, 72 for income statements, 75 for cash flows. These are the printed page numbers in the annual report section. It might be nice to include page, but there's risk the pagination doesn't match the exhibit's own pagination. The location schema allows page or html_anchor; I have html_anchor so page can be omitted. I'll omit page to avoid asserting uncertain pagination. Actually, wait — html_anchor must be non-null string. Fine.\n\nHmm, but is \"f-95\" truly an HTML anchor? In the source view these are inline XBRL fact ids. The safest interpretation: the anchor is the fact id in the ix markup. I'll use it.\n\nAlso for accounting_basis: US-GAAP — the auditor report says \"in conformity with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles\" and Note 1 says prepared in accordance with US GAAP. Good.\n\nValue formatting: \"2471\", \"58555\", \"3696\", \"36987\", \"58555\", \"4720\", \"7049\". All match pattern ^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(\\.[0-9]+)?$.\n\nScale \"1000000\" matches ^[1-9][0-9]*$.\n\nRequest ID: \"pilot-cni-exhibit-v1\".\n\nSchema: \"statement_candidate_v1\".\n\nOne more check on NetIncomeLoss — definition says \"Consolidated net income or loss explicitly reported on the primary income statement.\" The primary income statement is Consolidated Statements of Income. There are also Net income lines on the comprehensive income statement and cash flow statement — all 4,720 for 2025, consistent, so no ambiguity. Cite the income statement.\n\nAlso check that ctx c-4 is indeed 2025-12-31: Total assets f-107 ctx=c-4 = 58,555 and 2024 (c-5) = 57,067; the columns show 2025 first. The balance sheet header C6.2.3 \"2025\" C6.2.4 \"2024\". And f-85 (Cash ctx=c-4) = 350 in 2025 column. Yes.\n\nAnd c-1 for durations = 2025: Revenue f-1 ctx=c-1 = 17,304 in the 2025 column. Yes.\n\nEverything checks out. Now compose the JSON output. Only JSON, no extra text.\n\nLet me write evidence quotes precisely within 400 chars.\n\n1. AssetsCurrent:\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total current assets' shows 2,471 (2024: 2,619). Financial statements are expressed in Canadian dollars and prepared under U.S. GAAP.\"\n\n2. Assets:\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total assets' shows $ 58,555 (2024: $ 57,067).\"\n\n3. LiabilitiesCurrent:\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total current liabilities' shows 3,696 (2024: 3,976).\"\n\n4. Liabilities:\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total liabilities' shows 36,987 (2024: 36,016).\"\n\n5. LiabilitiesAndStockholdersEquity:\n\"CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS, 'In millions ... As at December 31, 2025': row 'Total liabilities and shareholders' equity' shows $ 58,555 (2024: $ 57,067).\"\n\n6. NetIncomeLoss:\n\"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME, 'In millions, except per share data ... Year ended December 31, 2025': row 'Net income' shows $ 4,720 (2024: $ 4,448; 2023: $ 5,625).\"\n\n7. NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities:\n\"CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF CASH FLOWS, 'In millions ... Year ended December 31, 2025': row 'Net cash provided by operating activities' shows 7,049 (2024: 6,699; 2023: 6,965).\"\n\nSource labels:\n1. \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total current assets\"\n2. \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total assets\"\n3. \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total current liabilities\"\n4. \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total liabilities\"\n5. \"Consolidated Balance Sheets – Total liabilities and shareholders' equity\"\n6. \"Consolidated Statements of Income – Net income\"\n7. \"Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows – Net cash provided by operating activities\"\n\nNow output the JSON.","tools":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":228315,"total_tokens":235290,"completion_tokens":6975,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4792},"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4792}}}